WEBVTT

00:12.000 --> 00:17.400
Ever since you began to build your empire,
you have had a crutch to lean on.

00:17.480 --> 00:19.640
[Michael] Mum, I swear
in the name of Almighty God,

00:19.720 --> 00:21.840
I will take revenge on Tommy Shelby.

00:21.920 --> 00:25.480
That, my friend,
is the finest opium in the world.

00:25.560 --> 00:28.960
Perhaps we can meet after you've
spoken to your wife's uncle, Jack Nelson.

00:29.040 --> 00:31.360
Tommy Shelby wants
to do business with Jack Nelson?

00:31.440 --> 00:33.840
So speak to your uncle
and get me out of here.

00:33.920 --> 00:37.280
If he doesn't want to buy my opium,
I will sell to the East Boston Jews.

00:37.360 --> 00:39.040
It's Ruby, she's not well.

00:39.120 --> 00:40.160
I'm coming home.

00:46.120 --> 00:50.880
[Polly] There will be a war in this family
and one of you will die.

00:52.280 --> 00:55.160
[Michael] You've been too busy
to punish the people who killed her.

00:56.000 --> 00:57.160
How is the family?

01:08.200 --> 01:09.239
[Ruby] Daddy!

01:13.960 --> 01:15.600
Hello, Ruby.

01:15.680 --> 01:16.680
[Ruby laughs]

01:16.760 --> 01:17.680
[Tommy] Come here.

01:18.200 --> 01:21.760
Let me see you. I missed you.
I missed you.

01:23.680 --> 01:27.040
-That's the Black Madonna. [kisses]
-[Charles] What presents did you get us?

01:27.120 --> 01:28.080
[Tommy] Son.

01:29.640 --> 01:32.440
She's all better, Tommy.
You came back for nothing.

01:36.240 --> 01:37.520
But I'm glad you're back.

01:39.680 --> 01:43.400
Right, before we do anything else,
we're going to go out for a drive.

01:43.480 --> 01:45.480
-Okay? Let's go.
-What about me?

01:45.560 --> 01:47.560
Yeah, you come too. Come on.

01:47.640 --> 01:48.680
A drive where?

01:49.800 --> 01:52.240
I've asked the driver
to take us to see Dr Robert.

01:52.320 --> 01:54.200
-To have a look at Ruby.
-Why?

01:54.280 --> 01:57.560
The appointment is in one hour.
You can stay here or you can come.

01:58.720 --> 01:59.680
Right.

02:01.320 --> 02:02.680
[Tommy] Right. Let's go.

02:22.480 --> 02:24.040
[children playing]

02:40.840 --> 02:41.760
[grunts]

02:42.920 --> 02:44.320
[gags and spits]

02:45.560 --> 02:46.600
[coughs]

02:50.240 --> 02:52.680
[door creaks open and shuts]

02:52.760 --> 02:53.680
[Lizzie] Tommy?

02:54.760 --> 02:55.680
Yeah?

02:58.120 --> 03:00.560
It was all good. Everything was clear.

03:00.640 --> 03:01.800
[exhales]

03:01.880 --> 03:03.120
That is a relief.

03:04.520 --> 03:06.080
-That's a relief.
-Yeah.

03:07.520 --> 03:09.360
-Driver's bringing the car around.
-[Ruby] Dad.

03:11.520 --> 03:12.520
[Lizzie] Hiya.

03:15.840 --> 03:16.880
Come here.

03:23.520 --> 03:24.760
When did you last sleep?

03:27.280 --> 03:29.440
Not much since we last spoke on the phone.

03:30.960 --> 03:33.400
Now you know Ruby is all clear,
you can sleep.

03:33.480 --> 03:34.480
Yeah.

03:37.040 --> 03:40.320
Lizzie, I'm very happy
that Ruby's results are clear.

03:40.840 --> 03:42.480
But still you won't sleep.

03:44.160 --> 03:47.000
I will speak to Johnny
and I will speak to Esmeralda.

03:47.080 --> 03:48.120
[sighs]

03:52.320 --> 03:54.280
[sighs] We could be on holiday.

03:55.440 --> 03:57.320
We could be up a mountain in America.

03:58.560 --> 04:00.240
That wouldn't have been possible.

04:01.120 --> 04:04.880
The man I'm dealing with
is coming to London. I need to be there.

04:05.440 --> 04:07.280
[exhales] No escape.

04:08.920 --> 04:10.400
We will escape, Lizzie.

04:10.960 --> 04:12.400
One last deal to be done.

04:13.120 --> 04:14.080
It'll be difficult.

04:14.160 --> 04:16.200
-[Lizzie sighs]
-Difficulties are to be expected.

04:16.280 --> 04:18.840
This is why I must move from item to item.

04:24.279 --> 04:25.360
Do you feel that?

04:26.480 --> 04:27.560
Do you feel anything?

04:29.160 --> 04:32.320
You know, you talk as if
you're watching everything on a screen.

04:36.560 --> 04:40.480
When we go home… When we go home,
we'll give the kids to Frances,

04:40.560 --> 04:42.320
and then you and me will go to bed.

04:43.840 --> 04:45.840
And I will be the next item.

04:46.560 --> 04:48.680
-That's how it feels now, Tommy.
-[sighs] Yeah.

04:48.760 --> 04:50.200
Everything on a list.

04:56.240 --> 04:58.200
-Hey, baby.
-[Ruby] When are we going home?

05:02.840 --> 05:04.040
[thunder rumbling]

05:07.720 --> 05:08.560
[glass shatters]

05:09.040 --> 05:10.360
[thunder cracks]

05:19.000 --> 05:20.720
[Lizzie] Tommy? Tommy?

05:22.520 --> 05:24.040
[both grunting]

05:34.640 --> 05:36.560
[Lizzie] Tommy? Tommy, what's happened?

05:37.400 --> 05:41.240
Oh, fuck! Fuck! Fuck! Fuck!

05:41.320 --> 05:43.280
-[Tommy grunting]
-Come here, come here.

05:44.000 --> 05:44.840
[Tommy gasps]

05:44.920 --> 05:46.240
[Lizzie] What's happening?

05:48.120 --> 05:49.000
Tommy!

05:54.080 --> 05:55.160
-Love.
-[both gasping]

06:06.640 --> 06:07.960
[exhales sharply]

06:12.480 --> 06:18.600
It is four years,
one month, six days, since I had a drink.

06:20.240 --> 06:21.360
My head is clear.

06:23.640 --> 06:24.760
I am myself.

06:27.040 --> 06:28.520
Is this the first time?

06:31.160 --> 06:33.360
Once on the ship back. Not as bad.

06:36.440 --> 06:37.440
Tommy.

06:39.040 --> 06:40.800
You need to see a doctor.

06:42.680 --> 06:43.960
I have work to do.

06:45.280 --> 06:46.200
[scoffs]

06:46.280 --> 06:47.880
It's the work that's to blame.

06:49.000 --> 06:51.200
The people you meet,
the lies that you tell.

06:54.000 --> 06:56.960
We've got to keep going
until this Boston business is done.

06:58.040 --> 06:59.160
Then we rest.

07:01.040 --> 07:03.280
Then we Peaky Blinders fucking rest.

07:05.800 --> 07:06.640
[rain pattering]

07:07.240 --> 07:10.880
[woman] Comrades,
before we end this planning meeting

07:10.960 --> 07:12.520
and send you out into the rain…

07:12.600 --> 07:13.720
[crowd laughing]

07:13.800 --> 07:15.080
…we have a surprise.

07:16.080 --> 07:19.240
He just arrived back
from a trade mission to America.

07:19.320 --> 07:24.240
He came back early and he has insisted
on addressing you volunteers in person.

07:24.320 --> 07:25.280
[crowd exclaims]

07:25.360 --> 07:28.720
[woman] Comrades, your Labour
representative for South Birmingham,

07:28.800 --> 07:31.560
-Mr Thomas Shelby, MP, OBE.
-[crowd cheering]

07:56.200 --> 07:57.400
I bring with me,

07:59.040 --> 08:04.360
on the train from London,
a message from Westminster.

08:05.920 --> 08:09.880
No! No, no, no. Not a message.
Not a message.

08:11.880 --> 08:13.840
An instruction, in fact.

08:13.920 --> 08:15.200
[crowd mutters]

08:16.120 --> 08:17.520
You must be silent.

08:17.600 --> 08:19.080
[crowd exclaims]

08:22.440 --> 08:23.920
You must say nothing!

08:25.680 --> 08:29.560
Say nothing
about the present situation in this city.

08:30.960 --> 08:32.480
Say nothing about hunger.

08:33.400 --> 08:36.880
Say nothing about jobs.
Say nothing about pay.

08:38.039 --> 08:42.159
But those in greener pastures,
they may speak.

08:42.240 --> 08:43.320
[crowd exclaims]

08:43.400 --> 08:45.240
They may raise their voices!

08:45.320 --> 08:46.360
[crowd shouts]

08:46.440 --> 08:49.039
But here in the smoke, you men and women,

08:49.120 --> 08:54.160
Irish and Italian and English,
who support the socialist cause…

08:54.760 --> 08:57.520
Even your socialist
cats and dogs and canaries…

08:57.600 --> 08:58.560
[crowd laughs]

09:00.040 --> 09:01.560
You must hush

09:01.640 --> 09:03.080
because the king

09:04.280 --> 09:06.360
and all the king's horses
and all the king's men…

09:06.440 --> 09:07.520
[crowd laughs]

09:07.600 --> 09:08.720
…want you to be silent.

09:10.600 --> 09:14.760
But it is you, my friends,
who must suffer the cuts in wages

09:14.840 --> 09:17.200
-and in welfare and in dignity!
-[crowd exclaims]

09:17.280 --> 09:20.680
And you must not complain
'cause that would be unpatriotic.

09:21.440 --> 09:26.640
You soldiers who have fought in France,
you are traitors if you speak up.

09:26.720 --> 09:31.360
You veterans of their wars
and their booms and their busts,

09:31.440 --> 09:35.040
it is you who must take the blows
and carry the burdens

09:35.120 --> 09:39.120
for the sake of those in greener pastures
who bellow at you…

09:39.200 --> 09:40.280
[slams fist]

09:41.160 --> 09:42.160
"Silence!"

09:42.240 --> 09:43.560
[crowd yells]

09:44.400 --> 09:45.880
Well, watch this, comrades.

09:46.520 --> 09:48.040
I will not be silent.

09:48.120 --> 09:49.000
[man] Never again.

09:49.080 --> 09:50.480
Not this Englishman.

09:50.560 --> 09:52.600
[crowd exclaims and cheers]

09:58.400 --> 10:00.280
No silence from me!

10:00.840 --> 10:04.080
No silence from me
because I have heard your voices

10:04.160 --> 10:08.600
when you come to me and tell me
about the cries of your hungry children.

10:10.080 --> 10:13.280
And I will gather up
every single one of those cries

10:13.360 --> 10:17.280
and I will take 'em with me
on the train back to Westminster.

10:18.200 --> 10:21.280
And I will let 'em out of the bag
in the House of Commons,

10:21.360 --> 10:23.680
and let them try and silence that, eh?

10:23.760 --> 10:25.640
[crowd cheers]

10:40.560 --> 10:43.520
[Tommy] Shouldn't that involve
some sharing of the burden?

10:44.720 --> 10:47.480
All of us taking
a smaller slice of the cake, eh?

10:48.560 --> 10:50.800
After all, it's bloody us
who bakes the cake

10:51.400 --> 10:53.960
and makes the cars and melts the metal.

10:55.160 --> 10:57.280
And the king, remember him?

10:58.400 --> 11:02.640
The man who ordered all of this.
Shouldn't he be taking some of the cuts?

11:03.680 --> 11:06.520
Some of the blows? Some of the pain?

11:07.360 --> 11:08.600
No or yes?

11:08.680 --> 11:09.800
[crowd exclaims] Yes!

11:20.680 --> 11:22.560
-[shushes]
-[exclaiming stops]

11:22.640 --> 11:24.560
Hush, you working men and women.

11:25.240 --> 11:26.440
Silence.

11:29.160 --> 11:30.160
Good.

11:31.080 --> 11:32.240
Save your voices.

11:33.840 --> 11:35.360
You're gonna need 'em

11:35.440 --> 11:39.560
on Saturday when we rally together,
at the Bull Ring Market!

11:39.640 --> 11:40.480
[crowd cheering]

11:40.560 --> 11:45.760
And together we will raise the roof,
break the damned silence,

11:47.880 --> 11:50.440
and bring down this broken government!

11:50.520 --> 11:52.000
[crowd cheering]

11:53.680 --> 11:59.720
[chanting] Tommy! Tommy! Tommy! Tommy!

12:06.760 --> 12:07.680
Thank you.

12:11.040 --> 12:12.200
Laura McKee.

12:13.440 --> 12:18.360
-Battalion Commander, Fermanagh, IRA.
-You missed the first and second act.

12:18.440 --> 12:21.120
-[woman] Thank you for coming, Mr Shelby.
-Thank you.

12:21.200 --> 12:22.680
[Laura] The third act was enough.

12:25.680 --> 12:29.880
You both have reasons to hate me and to
want to seek revenge for the killing--

12:29.960 --> 12:30.840
[shushes]

12:33.280 --> 12:34.520
Gypsy tradition.

12:36.160 --> 12:40.560
We do not mention the name
of the dead in company.

12:46.040 --> 12:51.720
Laura McKee, in the Shelby family,
business comes before issues of vengeance.

12:52.560 --> 12:55.640
Our beloved departed
would understand and approve.

12:57.440 --> 12:58.960
Let's go, boys.

12:59.040 --> 13:01.280
Our agreement was
we meet in a crowded place.

13:01.360 --> 13:02.680
No need for crowds.

13:03.880 --> 13:05.000
We need you alive.

13:07.720 --> 13:08.640
After you.

13:33.000 --> 13:36.560
You know, Mr Shelby, even though
we've been doing business for a while,

13:37.080 --> 13:38.560
we've never met in person.

13:40.040 --> 13:43.680
You spoke with passion and compassion.

13:46.120 --> 13:47.760
You understand forgiveness.

13:48.880 --> 13:50.120
And you drink water.

13:52.120 --> 13:55.080
Yet I heard from many reliable sources

13:55.160 --> 13:58.840
that you have a reputation
for moral turpitude.

13:59.960 --> 14:01.720
[chuckles and clicks tongue]

14:02.400 --> 14:03.720
"Moral turpitude."

14:05.640 --> 14:07.600
It's a good name for a racehorse.

14:08.760 --> 14:11.240
-You don't know what it means?
-I know what it means.

14:12.000 --> 14:13.520
It means you fuck people.

14:14.840 --> 14:16.960
Fuck people over. Don't give a fuck.

14:17.760 --> 14:20.720
It means you covet and steal
and burn all principles

14:20.800 --> 14:22.440
for the sake of self-interest.

14:24.440 --> 14:29.520
Well, I'm changing, Laura McKee.
And my organisation is also changing.

14:34.560 --> 14:36.200
So what happened in Boston?

14:37.280 --> 14:38.560
Jack Nelson said no.

14:39.360 --> 14:42.480
Are we accepting "no" as an answer?

14:44.240 --> 14:45.240
These are letters…

14:45.320 --> 14:46.160
[clears throat]

14:46.760 --> 14:50.240
…written to and by Jack Nelson
over the last three months.

15:03.520 --> 15:04.480
This…

15:05.920 --> 15:09.120
This is a private letter
from the president of the United States.

15:10.400 --> 15:12.000
Where the fuck did you get this?

15:12.080 --> 15:12.920
[Tommy sighs]

15:13.000 --> 15:17.880
My racehorse "Moral Turpitude"
is just one of many in my stables.

15:18.520 --> 15:21.000
Sometimes, even now,
I'll take her out for a run,

15:21.680 --> 15:24.240
if there is a good cause
that requires her services.

15:29.080 --> 15:30.760
Jack Nelson's coming to London.

15:31.760 --> 15:35.240
Officially, he's coming
to buy liquor import licences.

15:36.240 --> 15:38.520
Unofficially, he's on
a fact-finding mission.

15:40.080 --> 15:43.360
He's coming to measure the strength
of support for fascism in Britain.

15:43.440 --> 15:45.320
He'll report back to the president.

15:48.240 --> 15:49.640
And how does that help us?

15:52.920 --> 15:54.320
In this letter to his son,

15:55.560 --> 15:58.240
Jack Nelson expresses
strong support for fascism.

15:59.080 --> 16:00.000
In this letter,

16:01.080 --> 16:06.680
to a friend in Berlin, he says
some interesting things about Jews.

16:09.120 --> 16:11.200
He's not coming to Europe to find facts.

16:11.920 --> 16:14.480
He's coming to find proof
that fascism will prevail.

16:16.080 --> 16:20.320
And you and I
are going to help him in that task.

16:24.360 --> 16:25.960
I thought you were a socialist.

16:28.120 --> 16:29.120
[inhales]

16:29.640 --> 16:32.640
Well, since I've entered politics,

16:32.720 --> 16:37.440
I've learned that the line doesn't go out
from the middle to the left and the right.

16:37.520 --> 16:38.720
It goes in a circle.

16:40.080 --> 16:41.120
I'll show you.

16:44.800 --> 16:46.320
You go far enough left,

16:47.200 --> 16:50.440
eventually, you'll meet someone
who's gone far enough right

16:50.520 --> 16:52.040
to get to the same place.

16:54.840 --> 16:58.160
Working-class socialists like me,
working-class nationalists like you.

16:58.760 --> 16:59.840
The result…

17:00.560 --> 17:01.800
National Socialism.

17:04.080 --> 17:05.240
And that's me.

17:06.960 --> 17:08.080
In the middle.

17:09.599 --> 17:14.000
Just a man trying to make
an honest living in a very dark world.

17:18.359 --> 17:20.440
You have friends in Dublin, Laura McKee,

17:21.160 --> 17:23.680
who are actively fighting
for a fascist Ireland.

17:24.520 --> 17:27.480
And you are acting
on their behalf, ain't you?

17:29.440 --> 17:32.160
When Jack Nelson comes to London,

17:32.720 --> 17:37.960
I can give him access to Oswald Mosley
and to fascist sympathisers

17:38.640 --> 17:40.560
in the House of Commons
and the House of Lords.

17:40.640 --> 17:42.160
Both sides of the divide.

17:43.720 --> 17:45.240
Fascism is quite the thing

17:47.240 --> 17:48.880
among the very best people.

17:50.560 --> 17:54.200
And with your help,
I can also offer him Dublin.

17:58.200 --> 18:02.720
And you think this will allow us
to ship our merchandise to Boston?

18:02.800 --> 18:03.800
Perhaps.

18:04.680 --> 18:07.040
There may be other benefits
for your cause.

18:08.840 --> 18:10.800
All you have to do

18:10.880 --> 18:15.320
is sit with Jack Nelson and talk to him
about a new golden age,

18:16.080 --> 18:18.640
and let him put a pin
in the map of Ireland

18:18.720 --> 18:20.720
for the president of the United States.

18:21.640 --> 18:22.680
[thudding]

18:31.640 --> 18:33.800
I came to collect Arthur
and put him to bed.

18:34.840 --> 18:37.520
Found him in Garrison Lane
with a syringe in his hand.

18:38.160 --> 18:39.200
[sighs]

18:43.920 --> 18:45.360
"A friend loves at all time,

18:47.040 --> 18:48.720
a brother is born for adversity."

18:50.200 --> 18:51.720
Proverbs 17:17.

18:55.080 --> 18:56.800
Well, I have two brothers in need.

18:57.400 --> 19:00.040
But yours is the more urgent, Tommy.
Will you come with me?

19:03.400 --> 19:07.960
So, Laura McKee,
are you going to help me change the world?

19:10.320 --> 19:13.680
Mr Shelby, this meeting
is not what I expected.

19:14.320 --> 19:15.240
Never is.

19:16.480 --> 19:17.680
Is that a yes or a no?

19:20.840 --> 19:21.960
My answer is yes.

19:22.560 --> 19:23.400
[scoffs]

19:24.120 --> 19:25.400
The answer's always yes.

19:28.160 --> 19:30.720
[Tommy] The back door is unlocked.
You can let yourself out.

19:31.840 --> 19:35.960
And tell your friends back home,
Tommy Shelby has changed.

19:37.160 --> 19:39.560
[train screeching]

19:42.560 --> 19:43.720
[Tommy] Where is he?

19:43.800 --> 19:45.840
[Ada] When I found him,
the syringe was empty.

19:45.920 --> 19:48.520
He's sleeping it off on the cobbles.
Shit, Tommy.

19:48.600 --> 19:50.080
Shit.

19:50.160 --> 19:53.520
-It's all under control, Ada.
-I'm not under fucking control.

19:54.280 --> 19:57.920
I'm not you, Tommy.
And I'm not Polly either.

19:58.640 --> 20:00.240
Even though I'm trying to be.

20:00.320 --> 20:01.760
She would have stopped this.

20:01.840 --> 20:04.520
-We will pull Arthur through this.
-I'm not talking about Arthur.

20:04.600 --> 20:07.920
I'm talking about you. I heard
everything you were saying in there.

20:08.680 --> 20:11.040
Ada, this will be the end of it.

20:11.120 --> 20:14.640
Hear me? This is the way out for us.
And along the way, I will be doing good.

20:14.720 --> 20:17.280
No, along the way, you're gonna
make yourself a lot of money.

20:17.360 --> 20:18.960
All right, fair enough.

20:19.040 --> 20:22.120
Any incidental rewards
for my good work will be welcome.

20:22.200 --> 20:24.400
-But you will get your fair share, sister.
-[scoffs]

20:24.480 --> 20:28.200
And by being among the fascists,
by being among them, I can undermine them.

20:29.680 --> 20:30.920
Polly would approve.

20:32.120 --> 20:35.920
Beneath all the gold and diamonds
and fucking mink and lace,

20:36.000 --> 20:37.480
she was a solid socialist.

20:43.640 --> 20:46.200
[Ada] Look, I know
it's too late for this, Tom, but…

20:48.160 --> 20:49.600
This doorway…

20:49.680 --> 20:51.360
This same fucking doorway.

20:53.360 --> 20:55.720
We used to come here for Dad's beer.

20:55.800 --> 20:59.120
And we were so little,
it took two of us to carry one bucket.

21:02.040 --> 21:03.120
Yeah, I remember.

21:07.080 --> 21:08.440
Look at us now, eh?

21:09.120 --> 21:11.320
Yeah. Fucking look at us.

21:12.840 --> 21:13.960
Take a good look, Tom,

21:14.040 --> 21:16.360
'cause one of us
isn't gonna be here for long.

21:16.440 --> 21:19.480
Fuck! Opium and presidents.

21:26.560 --> 21:30.160
Ada, if you don't want
to help me carry the bucket…

21:32.960 --> 21:34.040
I wouldn't blame you.

21:36.880 --> 21:38.280
But this is my mission.

21:39.880 --> 21:41.520
And I will have no limitations.

21:45.280 --> 21:46.360
Where are you, Tom?

21:47.960 --> 21:48.840
Hmm?

21:49.760 --> 21:50.880
My big brother?

21:53.000 --> 21:55.320
You know, you used to stop
sometimes and laugh.

21:57.520 --> 21:59.240
Do you even remember this place?

22:01.040 --> 22:05.160
You walk into the Garrison like a stranger
and you sip fucking water.

22:09.800 --> 22:11.000
I'm alive, Ada.

22:13.440 --> 22:14.360
Yeah.

22:15.880 --> 22:18.560
And you're still looking for trouble
big enough to kill you.

22:21.400 --> 22:25.440
Well, I think you might have found it.

22:29.160 --> 22:30.720
I have children, Tommy.

22:32.680 --> 22:34.800
You have to carry this bucket on your own.

22:38.760 --> 22:41.320
One brother half-dead
in the rain in Garrison Alley,

22:41.400 --> 22:43.800
and the other has no limitations.

22:58.080 --> 22:59.520
[distant opera music]

23:10.600 --> 23:11.640
[lift thuds]

23:17.240 --> 23:18.320
[Tommy] I'm expected.

23:37.640 --> 23:38.680
[man] Oh.

23:38.760 --> 23:42.520
And Mr Solomons no longer tolerates
the smoking of tobacco in his presence.

23:47.360 --> 23:49.080
[opera playing over record player]

24:02.320 --> 24:03.840
[music crescendos]

24:22.960 --> 24:24.320
[music fades]

24:26.040 --> 24:27.080
[vinyl hiss]

24:27.160 --> 24:31.760
I always thought that opera
was just fat people fucking shouting.

24:31.840 --> 24:34.200
[Tommy] Yeah? What do you think now?

24:38.280 --> 24:40.880
[Alfie] I think the sound
of a tenor in full passion

24:40.960 --> 24:44.240
reminds me of
the crying out of Italian soldiers

24:44.320 --> 24:46.520
when they had my bayonet inside of them.

24:47.760 --> 24:53.240
Ever since my own death,
I have been somewhat haunted by it.

24:54.680 --> 24:55.880
Dear me.

24:58.920 --> 25:02.880
But, instead of fighting these voices,
I decided to write their songs down

25:02.960 --> 25:05.160
and turn them into an opera of my own.

25:05.720 --> 25:07.960
Do not light that. No, no.

25:08.560 --> 25:10.440
Were you not told I have a condition?

25:11.160 --> 25:12.760
What I was told, Alfie…

25:16.080 --> 25:21.800
is that you have withdrawn
and that you spend your days alone…

25:25.000 --> 25:27.520
obsessing about opera singers.

25:27.600 --> 25:29.320
[Alfie] Opera is not
fucking singing, is it?

25:31.840 --> 25:37.600
It's not singing. It's the sound
that people make before a word.

25:37.680 --> 25:41.760
And I do not allow smoking
because I do need to see fucking clearly.

25:42.800 --> 25:43.720
All right?

25:50.320 --> 25:53.120
What, do you sense
weakness in the Israelite?

25:53.200 --> 25:55.280
Not a sense of weakness, no, Alfie.

25:55.840 --> 25:57.320
A certain knowledge of it.

25:58.880 --> 26:02.720
Since you have been sat here
writing your opera…

26:05.280 --> 26:08.560
a member of your family has died.

26:10.080 --> 26:12.120
Charles Solomons, your uncle.

26:12.200 --> 26:14.320
He ran all the narcotics,

26:14.400 --> 26:18.160
bootlegging, prostitution,
gambling syndicates out of East Boston.

26:18.240 --> 26:20.720
But last January, poor old Charlie, well…

26:22.720 --> 26:27.120
He was shot in the Cotton Club,
in the lavatory,

26:27.920 --> 26:31.680
by men that you know,
and yet you did nothing, Alfie.

26:38.360 --> 26:40.880
Now my opera is called "America"!

26:41.720 --> 26:44.400
America is my fucking masterpiece!

26:44.920 --> 26:48.320
The truth is, your uncle is dead.

26:49.800 --> 26:50.920
Boston is gone.

26:52.280 --> 26:56.400
And you,
once the big man who ran Camden Town,

26:57.600 --> 27:02.400
now can't even extinguish
another man's cigarette.

27:05.200 --> 27:06.840
Let alone his fucking life.

27:07.760 --> 27:09.000
You need favours, Alfie.

27:09.080 --> 27:12.000
I need a fucking final act, right?

27:12.080 --> 27:15.560
Just a final fucking act for my opera.

27:16.760 --> 27:17.720
Yeah?

27:19.320 --> 27:20.200
Alfie,

27:21.960 --> 27:24.240
I think I may have written your final act.

27:26.320 --> 27:28.680
Why don't you sit down
and have a listen, eh?

27:53.080 --> 27:58.520
I have five tons of pure, refined opium,

27:59.360 --> 28:01.800
sitting in one of
my warehouses in Liverpool.

28:03.200 --> 28:06.840
I have safe storage
off the coast of Canada.

28:07.560 --> 28:11.240
I have men willing to distribute it

28:12.080 --> 28:15.520
in Toronto, Quebec, New York and Boston.

28:16.560 --> 28:18.120
The income would be immediate

28:19.040 --> 28:21.080
and will shift
the balance of power in Boston

28:21.160 --> 28:23.680
back in favour of the Solomons family.

28:23.760 --> 28:25.280
[Alfie exhales]

28:31.640 --> 28:35.040
In the final act
that I'm giving you, Alfie,

28:35.120 --> 28:37.320
it is you who takes the revenge.

28:40.560 --> 28:41.640
Why would you sell?

28:43.360 --> 28:46.520
The Irish are being difficult.
The Italians are not an option.

28:47.600 --> 28:49.560
Also, Alfie, you are my friend.

28:50.120 --> 28:52.080
-Would you give me credit?
-No.

28:53.520 --> 28:57.600
I will take property.
You own half the warehouses in Camden.

28:58.520 --> 29:00.200
I'll take 'em and knock 'em down.

29:00.280 --> 29:02.920
Build houses
for the needy and the deserving.

29:03.000 --> 29:03.960
Hmm. Oh.

29:06.000 --> 29:07.240
Hmm.

29:10.440 --> 29:12.040
Yeah, well, the…

29:12.920 --> 29:15.080
The Irish have always
been difficult, Tommy,

29:15.160 --> 29:18.200
they have for about fucking 700 years.

29:18.920 --> 29:19.760
[sniffs]

29:20.360 --> 29:22.880
You know that I once saw an Irishman

29:22.960 --> 29:28.280
arguing with the statue
of Oliver Cromwell in Parliament Square.

29:28.360 --> 29:30.360
The argument went on for quite a while.

29:30.440 --> 29:32.880
It went into the night
as his little voice echoed

29:32.960 --> 29:37.480
all around the Houses of Parliament
as he got more and more angered.

29:38.320 --> 29:40.840
Oliver Cromwell was reluctant, somewhat,

29:40.920 --> 29:43.120
to answer his legitimate questions.

29:43.200 --> 29:46.400
So angered, in fact, that eventually,

29:46.480 --> 29:52.640
he punched the statue on the nose
and broke his fucking hand.

29:54.200 --> 29:57.240
And there it is, you know,
the Irish Question.

29:58.640 --> 30:03.200
How come you can remember so much
about what happened 200 years ago,

30:03.280 --> 30:07.040
but you just can't remember
what fucking happened last night?

30:09.200 --> 30:10.520
[sighs]

30:14.680 --> 30:16.160
How much is a ton?

30:16.240 --> 30:17.120
[door opens]

30:18.120 --> 30:19.160
Johnny?

30:21.360 --> 30:22.280
[door shuts]

30:22.760 --> 30:23.960
Only me today.

30:27.600 --> 30:29.360
Jack says a few more weeks…

30:29.440 --> 30:30.440
[lock opens]

30:33.360 --> 30:34.800
…and you'll be free.

30:34.880 --> 30:36.360
When do you travel to London?

30:43.160 --> 30:44.200
Tomorrow.

30:46.120 --> 30:47.400
I came to say goodbye.

31:00.200 --> 31:03.760
When you go to London,
stay away from the Devil.

31:05.000 --> 31:07.400
Block your fucking ears if you have to.

31:07.480 --> 31:09.800
I'll be with you, Michael.

31:11.880 --> 31:13.400
I've been thinking about you.

31:17.280 --> 31:18.200
Only you.

31:23.200 --> 31:25.040
And don't worry about Tommy Shelby.

31:28.400 --> 31:30.160
I have no interest in a dead man.

31:34.400 --> 31:35.960
Jack says he has to die.

31:36.600 --> 31:38.080
Well, you tell Jack to wait.

31:39.440 --> 31:42.320
-If anyone's going to kill Tommy Shelby--
-It will be you.

31:43.480 --> 31:44.360
I know.

31:45.600 --> 31:46.720
I told Jack.

31:48.080 --> 31:52.000
And Jack said, "Okay, let the kid do it."

31:53.920 --> 31:58.240
And in return
he can collect the cash that Tommy won't.

32:00.720 --> 32:03.600
Five million dollars.

32:05.680 --> 32:06.840
The Devil will be dead.

32:08.800 --> 32:10.440
The future belongs to us.

32:12.080 --> 32:14.240
Oh, and, Michael…

32:17.640 --> 32:18.680
Every night,

32:20.080 --> 32:22.480
midnight in Boston, 5:00 a.m. in London,

32:24.320 --> 32:27.040
I'll be wide awake in my big, wide bed,

32:28.440 --> 32:30.840
and you'll be
wide awake in this prison cell.

32:33.440 --> 32:35.520
And our souls will come together.

32:35.600 --> 32:36.800
And we'll fuck.

32:39.120 --> 32:40.800
I won't need an alarm clock.

32:43.400 --> 32:45.280
And you won't sleep until I'm done.

32:46.320 --> 32:48.120
Midnight fucks, 5:00 a.m.

32:53.080 --> 32:54.120
Every day.

32:58.320 --> 32:59.920
Because we trust each other.

33:01.400 --> 33:02.600
Hmm.

33:10.680 --> 33:12.000
[clamouring]

33:38.400 --> 33:42.760
[man] You're a fucking traitor, Shelby!
You're a fucking scumbag! Bastard!

33:57.320 --> 33:58.240
[Mosley] Darker.

33:58.320 --> 33:59.280
[mechanical squeaking]

33:59.960 --> 34:00.800
Bluer.

34:02.520 --> 34:03.720
Sharper.

34:03.800 --> 34:04.720
[thudding]

34:04.800 --> 34:06.200
And also from below.

34:07.960 --> 34:09.240
Darling, how's that?

34:10.240 --> 34:13.159
You look absolutely terrifying, my love.

34:13.239 --> 34:14.560
[Mosley and Diana chuckle]

34:25.120 --> 34:26.199
Fuck lipstick.

34:29.199 --> 34:30.280
Fun.

34:34.159 --> 34:35.560
To launch the ship.

34:44.600 --> 34:46.920
To a long and terrible journey, Diana.

34:49.360 --> 34:51.159
Don't fucking let me down.

34:58.280 --> 35:00.880
[man] Mr Shelby? Mr Shelby?

35:01.520 --> 35:02.400
Daily Mirror.

35:02.960 --> 35:04.000
-Sir--
-Fuck off!

35:04.080 --> 35:07.800
May I ask why a socialist MP
would attend a fascist rally, sir?

35:07.880 --> 35:09.920
[Tommy] Let him in.
Let me answer the question.

35:11.160 --> 35:13.640
Mr Mosley's constituency borders my own.

35:13.720 --> 35:16.560
We've worked together in the past.
He was once a socialist himself.

35:17.120 --> 35:19.440
My role here tonight is to…

35:19.520 --> 35:22.800
To act as a bridge between ideologies.

35:23.400 --> 35:24.280
I'm in the middle.

35:24.840 --> 35:28.480
Mr Shelby, you once shared
a platform with Mr Mosley.

35:29.040 --> 35:31.120
Will you be sharing
the stage with him tonight?

35:31.200 --> 35:34.240
No. I'm simply here
to remind my friend, Mr Mosley,

35:34.320 --> 35:36.320
that the way of
the British people is compromise.

35:37.520 --> 35:38.840
You can print that, pal.

35:40.200 --> 35:41.480
Fucking rag.

35:43.800 --> 35:44.640
[Lizzie sighs]

35:47.760 --> 35:48.640
[Tommy sighs]

35:50.040 --> 35:53.160
Lizzie, you should know
that Mosley's wife died six months ago.

35:53.920 --> 35:56.000
So, give him your condolences, will you?

35:56.600 --> 36:02.000
Tonight, he'll be with his mistress,
who is apparently a lady of some standing,

36:03.880 --> 36:06.520
and has given him great comfort
in his time of grief.

36:08.160 --> 36:11.200
[Arthur] Fuck off, you dozy bastard!

36:11.760 --> 36:13.320
Move out of my fucking way!

36:13.400 --> 36:15.120
What is Arthur doing here?

36:15.200 --> 36:17.160
Mosley invited him. I agreed.

36:17.880 --> 36:21.600
Arthur made me a promise,
which he appears to have broken.

36:23.320 --> 36:24.400
[Arthur] Move!

36:24.480 --> 36:25.800
I said fucking move!

36:25.880 --> 36:28.240
-Move, I'm on the fucking list!
-I've tried my best.

36:28.320 --> 36:31.080
-[Arthur] Get the fuck off me!
-He's hid some junk in his sock.

36:31.160 --> 36:32.760
-Okay.
-[Arthur] Move it along!

36:32.840 --> 36:34.400
Get out of my fucking way!

36:34.960 --> 36:35.800
Oi!

36:35.880 --> 36:37.160
Tommy!

36:37.240 --> 36:38.480
-Come on. You're in.
-Tommy.

36:38.560 --> 36:40.080
[Tommy] You're in. Come on, you're in.

36:40.160 --> 36:42.600
-[Arthur] My brother, Tommy.
-[Tommy] Yep.

36:42.680 --> 36:44.200
[Arthur] Johnny Dogs.

36:44.280 --> 36:45.800
Mosley invited me.

36:45.880 --> 36:48.760
-He said, "Wear a black fucking shirt."
-Here you are.

36:48.840 --> 36:51.840
I said, "I'd look like
every other bastard."

36:51.920 --> 36:53.320
-Lizzie!
-Come on.

36:53.400 --> 36:55.320
[Arthur] You're an angel.

36:55.400 --> 36:57.600
I know I've fucking let you down.

36:57.680 --> 37:00.240
I've fucking let you down.
I know I have, all right?

37:00.320 --> 37:03.800
I've fucking said sorry a million times.
I'll say it again. I'm sorry.

37:03.880 --> 37:05.720
-[Tommy] Yep.
-[Arthur] Fucking sorry.

37:06.320 --> 37:09.680
Look at Johnny Dogs,
look at the fucking state of him.

37:09.760 --> 37:11.600
He looks like a fucking waiter.

37:11.680 --> 37:14.240
-[Dogs] Shut up!
-Get me a fucking drink.

37:14.320 --> 37:16.600
Johnny, take your shirt off
and give it to me.

37:16.680 --> 37:18.000
For fuck's sake, Tom.

37:18.080 --> 37:20.560
Take your fucking shirt off
and give it to me now.

37:20.640 --> 37:21.840
Get it off!

37:22.360 --> 37:24.760
Arthur, this is my fault.

37:25.840 --> 37:27.600
-This is my fault.
-Yeah.

37:27.680 --> 37:32.160
Remember, we voted on getting
involved in the opium trade, you voted no.

37:32.240 --> 37:33.720
-I said no.
-Remember?

37:34.280 --> 37:35.520
I overruled you.

37:36.240 --> 37:38.120
-I've been away.
-Where you been, Tom?

37:38.200 --> 37:40.280
Ada tells me you've been
hanging out with Mosley?

37:40.360 --> 37:41.920
-Yeah, in Smethwick.
-Yeah?

37:42.000 --> 37:44.440
At his big, beautiful fucking house.

37:44.520 --> 37:46.880
And they have parties there in Belgravia.

37:46.960 --> 37:49.120
And they give me fucking respect.

37:49.200 --> 37:52.560
And what do you give them?
Snow and junk from the company.

37:53.320 --> 37:56.600
Look at you, brother.
Half of you has gone.

37:58.200 --> 38:00.280
-[Arthur] The fuck!
-[Tommy] Rag and bone.

38:02.280 --> 38:04.080
You fucking slapped me.

38:06.080 --> 38:07.360
You slapped me.

38:08.160 --> 38:09.920
I have to remain unresolved.

38:10.000 --> 38:11.640
Do you understand? Unresolved.

38:11.720 --> 38:14.240
Unresolved in everything!

38:14.320 --> 38:17.240
I have to move between
left and right, light and shade,

38:17.320 --> 38:18.560
and maintain the trust of both.

38:18.640 --> 38:21.160
And I cannot have my brother
wearing a fucking black shirt

38:21.720 --> 38:23.120
on the cover of the Daily Mirror.

38:23.200 --> 38:25.560
If anyone takes my picture in this,

38:25.640 --> 38:28.400
they'll find their fucking camera
under my heel, Tom.

38:28.480 --> 38:30.520
They're throwing petrol bombs
out there, Tommy.

38:30.600 --> 38:33.400
-I thought Ada was taking care of you.
-Ada's got decisions to make

38:33.480 --> 38:34.800
about working with us.

38:35.520 --> 38:37.160
She doesn't know what she wants.

38:37.240 --> 38:38.320
I'll speak to Ada.

38:38.960 --> 38:41.440
-Listen, I'm going home--
-No, you stay there.

38:42.760 --> 38:44.040
I have something for you.

38:44.560 --> 38:47.120
Lizzie, you go with Johnny.
Johnny, take Lizzie to her seat.

38:47.200 --> 38:48.680
I don't have an invitation.

38:48.760 --> 38:51.640
You're wearing a black shirt,
you can do what you like. Go on.

38:51.720 --> 38:53.200
I'll follow you. Go on.

38:54.880 --> 38:55.880
Go on, Dogs.

38:56.520 --> 38:58.640
Get me a fucking drink while you're there.

39:00.640 --> 39:01.640
[groans]

39:01.720 --> 39:03.120
[distant music and cheering]

39:03.800 --> 39:05.320
I know, Tom, look at me.

39:05.400 --> 39:09.640
Arthur, before I went
to America, I wrote a letter.

39:10.320 --> 39:11.520
Yeah? Who to?

39:12.120 --> 39:13.120
To Linda.

39:16.160 --> 39:17.720
And in that letter, I wrote,

39:18.560 --> 39:24.440
"Linda, as a Christian woman,
do you believe in forgiveness?"

39:27.720 --> 39:29.000
This is what I got back.

39:30.000 --> 39:31.920
Two days ago. Have a look.

39:42.600 --> 39:45.880
"As a Christian woman,
I do believe in forgiveness."

39:45.960 --> 39:48.680
Yeah, and the word "do" is underlined.

39:52.400 --> 39:56.840
Arthur, I'm no Christian,
but I also believe in forgiveness.

39:59.360 --> 40:00.520
Get yourself clean.

40:01.560 --> 40:03.040
Stay clean for two weeks.

40:03.640 --> 40:05.360
I'll write Linda another letter.

40:08.560 --> 40:10.040
'Cause I know where she is.

40:13.840 --> 40:15.160
First, I need you back.

40:17.080 --> 40:18.280
I need my brother.

40:20.120 --> 40:21.320
I've a lot to do.

40:22.280 --> 40:23.960
Need someone to do the real work.

40:24.040 --> 40:27.440
Yeah, look at you smile, Tom.

40:28.000 --> 40:29.600
Look at your smile, brother.

40:29.680 --> 40:30.760
It's been so long.

40:30.840 --> 40:32.800
Come on, let's see
what this bastard has to say.

40:32.880 --> 40:33.800
Come on.

40:34.720 --> 40:36.560
-All right.
-Come on.

40:36.640 --> 40:38.160
[Arthur] Yeah, I'm coming.

40:38.240 --> 40:40.120
He is a bastard and all, Tommy.

40:40.200 --> 40:42.040
Black shirts and Jews. Here we go.

40:42.120 --> 40:43.840
Here we fucking go.

40:46.360 --> 40:48.480
You stay in the middle
and do nothing, Tom.

40:49.040 --> 40:50.320
But not fucking me!

40:50.920 --> 40:53.040
Me and you, you Nazi bastard!

40:53.120 --> 40:54.960
[men grunting]

41:02.400 --> 41:04.000
[Arthur] You! You!

41:09.320 --> 41:11.760
Come here, man.
I'll take your fucking eye.

41:11.840 --> 41:13.400
[Tommy] Not here! Not here!

41:13.480 --> 41:14.560
[grunts]

41:17.120 --> 41:18.680
Come here. You've had your fun.

41:18.760 --> 41:20.640
-Now let's go home.
-[Tommy] We have business.

41:20.720 --> 41:21.720
[Lizzie scoffs]

41:24.720 --> 41:26.720
[Tommy] Johnny, you get him home.

41:26.800 --> 41:29.040
This time, check his fucking socks.

41:35.240 --> 41:36.160
[Dogs] For fuck's sake.

41:42.600 --> 41:45.840
Tommy, we should get out now.
Forget this American business.

41:45.920 --> 41:47.480
We've got enough.

41:47.560 --> 41:48.800
Not yet enough.

41:48.880 --> 41:49.880
Here she comes.

41:49.960 --> 41:51.040
Remember to smile.

41:51.120 --> 41:52.640
-Come on.
-Shit.

41:57.120 --> 41:58.200
[glass clinks]

42:02.480 --> 42:07.480
Ladies and gentlemen, tonight,
he has truly earned your adulation.

42:07.560 --> 42:12.080
The future prime minister
of this great country, Sir Oswald Mosley.

42:12.160 --> 42:13.240
[crowd applauding]

42:16.400 --> 42:17.560
[man] Fuck you, Mosley!

42:41.520 --> 42:43.200
[crowd applauding]

42:49.960 --> 42:51.080
Fuck. I look terrible.

42:51.160 --> 42:53.800
You look beautiful, Lizzie.
I need to impress this woman,

42:53.880 --> 42:56.120
so I will act as if
she is beautiful as well.

42:57.560 --> 42:58.440
Mosley.

43:01.160 --> 43:06.560
Diana, this is Tommy Shelby, MP, OBE.

43:07.080 --> 43:09.000
Mr Shelby, Lady Diana Mitford.

43:09.080 --> 43:11.560
Oswald's most recent
and last ever mistress.

43:12.160 --> 43:14.320
And this is my wife, Lizzie Shelby.

43:14.400 --> 43:15.560
Beautiful earrings.

43:15.640 --> 43:17.080
[Tommy] I stole them from Tiffany's.

43:17.160 --> 43:20.960
Actually, he bought the earrings in Paris.
We were in Paris on our honeymoon.

43:21.040 --> 43:23.080
-God, I hate Paris.
-[Tommy] Mmm.

43:23.640 --> 43:24.760
I hear you prefer Berlin.

43:24.840 --> 43:27.480
Oswald and I are going
to marry there, aren't we, Oswald?

43:29.480 --> 43:31.280
Mosley, I have business to discuss.

43:31.360 --> 43:34.200
Perhaps you and I
could find somewhere a bit quieter, eh?

43:35.880 --> 43:39.320
Darling, Mr Shelby just made
the astonishing suggestion

43:39.400 --> 43:41.280
that we men go off and discuss business

43:41.360 --> 43:43.400
while you women
wait around looking glamorous.

43:43.480 --> 43:48.480
[laughs] Goodness. What year do you
think this is, Mr Shelby, 1807?

43:48.560 --> 43:51.400
In Birmingham,
the centuries grind by quite slowly.

43:53.000 --> 43:57.320
But, Mr Shelby, if it's business,
Diana is the engine of my enterprise.

43:57.400 --> 43:59.640
It's the modern way, Mr Shelby.

43:59.720 --> 44:02.520
Yes, we know. I am company director.

44:02.600 --> 44:03.960
I will join the meeting as well.

44:04.040 --> 44:06.560
But of course,
you must come as well, Elizabeth.

44:06.640 --> 44:10.880
By the way, I really don't like "Lizzie."
I prefer "Liberated Elizabeth."

44:10.960 --> 44:12.440
She must be part of this.

44:12.520 --> 44:15.720
She's been all the way to Paris,
so she is a woman of the world. Bravo.

44:16.320 --> 44:19.080
Do you know,
Oswald's told me everything about you.

44:31.600 --> 44:32.760
[Mosley] Only three

44:34.160 --> 44:36.360
because I know
these days Mr Shelby doesn't.

44:36.440 --> 44:38.280
[Diana] Our friend in Berlin
doesn't either.

44:38.840 --> 44:40.520
Well, they have that in common, at least.

44:40.600 --> 44:42.520
[Diana] I imagine
they have lots in common.

44:42.600 --> 44:43.720
[Mosley] Hmm.

44:45.000 --> 44:45.960
[smacks lips]

44:46.040 --> 44:47.440
Report to me, Shelby.

44:48.480 --> 44:51.960
Officially, Jack Nelson is in London
to buy import licences.

44:55.280 --> 44:57.880
And unofficially, he's Roosevelt's envoy.

44:59.240 --> 45:01.320
[Tommy] As you can see
from this private letter,

45:03.080 --> 45:05.120
he is far from a neutral point of view.

45:09.560 --> 45:11.360
Look at the bottom
of the second paragraph.

45:11.920 --> 45:14.760
"Individually, Jews are fine,
but as a race, they stink."

45:15.800 --> 45:16.640
[Mosley] Hmm.

45:17.560 --> 45:18.720
Elizabeth,

45:18.800 --> 45:22.320
do you even know why the bridge
to President Roosevelt is so important?

45:25.520 --> 45:27.920
Actually, no.

45:28.000 --> 45:30.360
I don't really know
much about this business at all.

45:32.760 --> 45:33.640
[glass thuds]

45:35.400 --> 45:37.560
But I have fucked your future husband.

45:38.280 --> 45:40.160
So I know lots of things about him.

45:43.040 --> 45:44.440
Tommy, I'll be outside.

45:45.880 --> 45:47.240
Well done, Elizabeth.

45:49.400 --> 45:51.360
-[door closes]
-[Tommy clears throat]

45:51.440 --> 45:53.480
Do you people want to meet Nelson or no?

45:55.040 --> 45:56.080
Mr Shelby…

45:56.880 --> 45:58.760
From now on, can I call you Thomas?

45:58.840 --> 46:00.080
[Tommy] If you like.

46:00.160 --> 46:03.840
Of course we would.
And we are very grateful for your efforts.

46:04.600 --> 46:09.240
[Mosley] But, Mr Shelby,
before this enterprise goes any further,

46:09.800 --> 46:12.280
you really must
do something about your wife.

46:40.000 --> 46:41.280
Mr Shelby?

46:42.160 --> 46:44.320
Yes. Mr Nelson.

46:45.320 --> 46:46.600
I came early.

46:47.600 --> 46:50.840
I wanted to come and take a look
around this beautiful church.

46:53.200 --> 46:54.960
You're Catholic, Mr Shelby?

46:56.400 --> 46:58.800
I hoped that by suggesting
we meet in church,

46:58.880 --> 47:03.240
it might make us both
more cautious with lies and truth.

47:04.640 --> 47:06.600
Well, then, your hope would be forlorn.

47:08.400 --> 47:10.440
There ain't no one listening here.

47:10.520 --> 47:12.000
You don't believe in God?

47:12.080 --> 47:13.120
No.

47:16.400 --> 47:20.080
It was the way the Catholics are treated
in my country that made me angry.

47:21.880 --> 47:23.360
Made me what I became.

47:27.480 --> 47:28.640
What made you angry?

47:31.920 --> 47:34.880
Slowness in anything.

47:36.960 --> 47:39.760
I wanted to have everything already.

47:42.640 --> 47:44.720
Two working-class Catholic boys.

47:48.760 --> 47:50.920
Did they mess with you
when you were small?

47:52.160 --> 47:53.760
Some man in the shadows.

47:55.800 --> 47:57.680
I carried a screwdriver and a blade.

47:58.840 --> 48:01.400
And everyone believed
I had the power to lay curses.

48:01.960 --> 48:03.000
[Nelson] And do you?

48:03.800 --> 48:05.040
[Tommy] Yes, I do.

48:08.160 --> 48:10.480
[Nelson] First man I killed was a priest.

48:12.600 --> 48:13.520
You?

48:14.920 --> 48:19.280
[Tommy] A Prussian boy with green eyes,
who was already underground.

48:19.360 --> 48:21.440
[Nelson] When'd you last kill
a man, Mr Shelby?

48:26.400 --> 48:27.600
[Tommy] Four years ago.

48:30.320 --> 48:31.880
His name was Tommy Shelby.

48:33.560 --> 48:34.920
He drank whiskey.

48:37.560 --> 48:44.120
You want me to allow you to enter my city
and deal narcotics that'll kill people?

48:48.120 --> 48:51.120
You deal in whiskey, Mr Nelson.

48:52.640 --> 48:55.160
I recently read a report,
by the Vatican, actually,

48:56.120 --> 48:59.000
which said that whiskey
disproportionately kills

48:59.080 --> 49:01.120
more of our Catholic brothers and sisters.

49:01.200 --> 49:02.240
Whereas opium

49:03.440 --> 49:08.120
is the sedative more often chosen
by Protestants and atheists.

49:11.240 --> 49:14.600
In return, there are people in England
who you think I should meet?

49:14.680 --> 49:15.520
Yes.

49:16.200 --> 49:17.240
Yes. Like minds.

49:20.200 --> 49:24.120
I'm here to buy import licences for booze.

49:26.040 --> 49:27.840
The booze of the blue blood elite.

49:29.160 --> 49:30.760
In America, we…

49:30.840 --> 49:32.000
We like labels.

49:32.960 --> 49:34.400
And aspiration.

49:34.480 --> 49:38.120
Well, I have a brand
of my own vodka and gin.

49:39.000 --> 49:40.760
You can add that to your portfolio.

49:41.880 --> 49:44.920
I hear Shelby labels
are favoured by the working class.

49:45.640 --> 49:47.760
Indeed. A fact of which I'm very proud.

49:48.360 --> 49:51.240
They say you're a poet too?

49:51.840 --> 49:53.800
No. I only read it.

49:56.080 --> 49:59.520
There are some people in this country
who I'd like to meet.

50:03.840 --> 50:04.760
Fascists.

50:04.840 --> 50:08.800
Not the ones in boots and black shirts.
The ones in tuxedos.

50:11.160 --> 50:13.040
I know men who are friends of the cause.

50:13.760 --> 50:16.000
I also know men
who are enemies of the cause.

50:17.640 --> 50:20.720
For many years now, I've been working
closely with Winston Churchill

50:20.800 --> 50:22.280
in many different capacities.

50:23.040 --> 50:24.040
I have his trust.

50:25.040 --> 50:27.440
He's opposed to the rise of fascism.

50:27.520 --> 50:30.080
You, I believe, see it as inevitable.

50:32.160 --> 50:35.400
Well, I can give you men of influence
who support your cause.

50:36.280 --> 50:39.920
I can also offer you a full report
on Churchill's strategies.

50:43.960 --> 50:46.800
All this in return
for access to South Boston?

50:47.880 --> 50:53.520
Alternatively, you can take on Churchill
on your own without my intelligence.

50:54.520 --> 50:56.480
And I can sell my opium to the Jews.

51:01.600 --> 51:03.800
You're a brave man, Mr Shelby.

51:05.720 --> 51:07.280
A war hero, I hear.

51:09.400 --> 51:10.800
Every war hero I ever met,

51:10.880 --> 51:13.400
they're just someone
who wanted to get themselves killed.

51:13.480 --> 51:14.440
[chuckles]

51:17.440 --> 51:19.240
Do we have a deal, Mr Nelson?

51:24.400 --> 51:26.920
I'll think a great deal
about what you've said.

51:40.840 --> 51:43.200
Ruby, have you finished
your spelling, love?

51:59.000 --> 52:02.480
Ruby? Ruby?

52:08.920 --> 52:09.800
Ruby?

52:14.320 --> 52:17.640
Ruby? What are you doing, love?

52:18.680 --> 52:20.160
I can hear voices.

52:21.600 --> 52:23.120
Coming from up the chimney.

52:26.880 --> 52:28.040
What voices?

52:28.120 --> 52:29.280
The grey man.

52:34.520 --> 52:35.400
[man] Gentlemen,

52:35.480 --> 52:39.000
Mr Thomas Shelby, Birmingham South.

52:42.040 --> 52:47.320
Mister Speaker, I was raised in a family
that endured living conditions

52:47.400 --> 52:50.200
that would test the morality
of even the most virtuous.

52:51.480 --> 52:55.000
Indeed, even the best of us
would have our virtues

52:55.080 --> 52:58.080
trounced and thwarted
by life and the meanness

52:58.160 --> 53:01.240
and the bitterness
of an overcrowded British slum.

53:01.320 --> 53:03.360
What would you know about virtue?

53:03.440 --> 53:04.960
[clamouring]

53:10.280 --> 53:11.600
[Lizzie] Quickly, please.

53:11.680 --> 53:13.000
[Lizzie breathing heavily]

53:13.600 --> 53:17.120
Therefore, Mister Speaker,
I intend to put before this house

53:17.200 --> 53:22.920
a bill which will offer radical reform
in housing policy in this country,

53:23.000 --> 53:25.040
in which slums are cleared,

53:25.120 --> 53:30.320
new houses are built,
with new standards in health and hygiene.

53:34.160 --> 53:37.040
Westminster 245. House of Commons.

53:37.600 --> 53:39.280
[telephone ringing]

53:42.160 --> 53:44.920
The time has come for change.
The people have had enough.

53:45.000 --> 53:45.880
[giggles]

53:45.960 --> 53:48.760
Let's open the windows, let in new light,

53:48.840 --> 53:53.400
build a new Jerusalem,
brick by government-owned brick.

53:53.480 --> 53:55.360
[all cheering]

53:59.200 --> 54:00.160
Into there.

54:00.240 --> 54:01.160
[Ruby coughing]

54:04.920 --> 54:05.760
Good.

54:10.600 --> 54:11.520
Doctor?

54:15.600 --> 54:17.120
Yeah, Westminster 245.

54:21.880 --> 54:22.800
Mr Shelby.

54:42.480 --> 54:45.800
[Lizzie] "Tickner Maura, O Beng, O Beng,"
over and over again.

54:45.880 --> 54:48.360
-[Michael] How is the family?
-[Polly] One of you will die.

54:48.440 --> 54:51.360
-[Ruby] He's staring at me, Daddy.
-[Lizzie] A man with green eyes.

54:52.320 --> 54:54.120
Can you stop the voices?

54:55.760 --> 54:57.680
[Lizzie] There are no voices, my love.

54:58.520 --> 54:59.800
[Ruby] It's the grey man.

55:01.200 --> 55:02.840
He says he's coming for me.

55:04.520 --> 55:06.360
And he's coming for Daddy as well.

55:29.920 --> 55:32.080
-[man grunts]
-[Tommy gasps]

55:43.800 --> 55:46.040
[telephone ringing]

55:53.880 --> 55:56.080
[both grunting]

55:56.160 --> 55:57.280
[man yells]

56:07.800 --> 56:10.960
-[knife pierces]
-[screams]

56:19.120 --> 56:20.520
[knock on door]

56:20.600 --> 56:21.880
[man] Mr Shelby?

56:22.920 --> 56:25.080
Is everything all right in there?

56:27.160 --> 56:28.000
[knocking continues]

56:28.080 --> 56:29.120
Mr Shelby?

56:29.920 --> 56:33.480
Everything's fine. Everything's fine.

56:35.240 --> 56:37.240
[telephone ringing]

56:46.440 --> 56:47.800
-Hello?
-[Lizzie] Tommy?

56:47.880 --> 56:50.800
Tommy. She has a temperature
of 101 and nothing is working.

56:50.880 --> 56:52.760
-Just get here now.
-Lizzie?

56:52.840 --> 56:54.160
-Please.
-Lizzie--

56:56.440 --> 56:57.560
[sighs]

56:59.400 --> 57:02.600
[breathes heavily]

57:18.280 --> 57:19.160
Where is she?

57:19.240 --> 57:20.800
She's with the doctor upstairs.

57:23.440 --> 57:24.480
Listen, Tommy.

57:25.760 --> 57:28.080
He said we shouldn't
come close to her in case…

57:28.160 --> 57:29.160
In case of what?

57:30.160 --> 57:31.760
When she coughs, there's blood.

57:49.840 --> 57:56.360
Madonna, put me through to the number
I gave you for Esme Shelby-Lee.
